monitor: re-blur the background after a soft rule apply

applyMonitorRuleSoft installs a new transform (transform is a soft
prop, so rotating an output through monitor rules lands here) and
recomputes the matrix and damage size, but never marks the monitor's
pre-blurred background cache dirty. With decoration:blur:new_optimizations
(the default), tiled windows blur from that cache, so after a rotation
the wallpaper itself re-renders in the new orientation while the blur
behind every window keeps showing the old one.

Confirmed on a rotated laptop panel: the stale blur persisted until a
blur config change (which sets m_blurFBDirty) was made, at which point
it matched immediately. Mark it dirty on every soft apply.

--- a/src/output/Monitor.cpp	2026-09-28 16:55:13.560695212 +0900
+++ b/src/output/Monitor.cpp	2026-09-28 16:55:13.649737099 +0900
@@ -712,6 +712,14 @@
 
     m_damage.setSize(m_transformedSize);
 
+    // The pre-blurred background cache (decoration:blur:new_optimizations)
+    // was rendered under the previous transform, and nothing on this path
+    // invalidates it -- after a transform-only rule apply (rotation), windows
+    // kept blurring an un-rotated wallpaper until some unrelated event
+    // happened to dirty it. Soft applies are rare, so re-blurring on every
+    // one costs nothing measurable.
+    m_blurFBDirty = true;
+
     setMirror(m_activeMonitorRule.m_mirrorOf);
 
     return true;
